# MM Architecture Gate

Before any Materials Management change in matching paths:

1. Align with `docs/MASTER_ENTERPRISE_SYSTEM_FLOW.md` (enterprise ownership; MM as material + inventory).
2. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/materials-management/SKILL.md` (permanent MM contract).
3. Inspect existing code in `backend/src/mm/` and `src/modules/mm/` before proposing changes.
4. Read `docs/MM_DEPENDENCY_MAP.md` for MM-01→15 build order and document ownership.
5. Read focused architecture docs as needed:
   - `docs/MM_ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md` — governance + allowed patterns (Phase 6)
   - `docs/MM_FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS.md` — forbidden catalog + rule IDs
   - `docs/MM_ARCHITECTURE.md` — posting invariant and service map
   - `docs/MM_DOMAIN_BOUNDARIES.md` — ownership matrix
   - `docs/MM_TRANSACTION_RULES.md` — ledger, movement types, idempotency
   - `docs/MM_QUALITY_RULES.md` / `docs/MM_MRP_RULES.md` / `docs/MM_INTEGRATION_RULES.md`
   - `docs/MM_INTEGRATION_CONTRACTS.md` — cross-module events
   - `docs/MM_QUALITY_ARCHITECTURE.md` — inspection / usage decisions
   - `docs/MM_MRP_ARCHITECTURE.md` — planning-only rules
6. Run `npm run test:architecture` in `backend/` after MM backend changes.
7. Prefer reusing `InventoryPostingService` for all physical stock changes.
8. Preserve: Receiving → Goods Receipt → Inventory Posting Service → Inventory Ledger.
9. Do not invent parallel engines, duplicate GR paths, or frontend stock math.
10. Keep UI on ECME + existing shared components; thin app routes under `src/app/(protected-pages)/modules/mm/`.
11. Extended detail: `.cursor/skills/materials-management/reference.md`.
